- a transactions-only split query can be upsampled if the user's query text contained `event.type:error`."}, {"file": "src/sentry/api/helpers/error_upsampling.py", "line": 38, "severity": "medium", "category": "data", "title": "Eligibility cache is never invalidated and contradicts its own documentation", "body": "Eligibility is cached for 60s per org and project set. `invalidate_upsampling_cache` is defined but never called, even though its docstring says it should run when the allowlist changes. As a result, allowlist changes take up to 60s to apply, and different hosts can return different counts for the same query in that window. The docstring on `_are_all_projects_error_upsampled` also claims the configuration is read fresh each time, which the cache makes false. Either wire up invalidation or drop the cache."}, {"file": "src/sentry/api/helpers/error_upsampling.py", "line": 27, "severity": "low", "category": "perf", "title": "Cache adds a remote round-trip in front of an already-cached option lookup", "body": "The code claims `options.get` is an expensive lookup. In practice options are cached in-process, so `options.get` is cheap. Putting `cache.get` / `cache.set` in front of it adds a memcached or redis round-trip to every `_get_event_stats` call, which makes the request slower rather than faster. The key is also built from Python `hash()` of the project tuple, so two different project sets can collide and share an eligibility result."}, {"file": "src/sentry/search/events/datasets/discover.py", "line": 1048, "severity": "medium", "category": "data", "title": "upsampled_count silently drops events without sample_weight", "body": "`upsampled_count` is defined as `toInt64(sum(sample_weight))` with no fallback. Events that have no sample_weight contribute nothing to the sum. That includes events ingested before a project was allowlisted, or events whose SDK sent no client sample rate. Once a project is allowlisted, historical or unsampled error counts drop toward 0 instead of counting as 1 each. Use something like `sum(ifNull(sample_weight, 1))`. The result type is also declared `number` while `count()` is `integer`, which changes the response meta for the same yAxis."}, {"file": "tests/sentry/api/helpers/test_error_upsampling.py", "line": 77, "severity": "low", "category": "test_gap", "title": "Missing tests for caching path and negated filters", "body": "There are no tests for:
